          %h3#higher_klein_geometry Higher Klein geometry
          %p
            Aspects of Klein geometry may be generalized from groups to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            and even
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} categories
            or
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"} groupoids
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Klein+geometry"} higher Klein geometry
          %h3#logicality_and_invariance Logicality and invariance
          %p
            Logicians have attempted to demonstrate that specifically
            %em logical
            constructions are those invariant under the largest group of transformations, in the sense of the Erlangen program. See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logicality+and+invariance"} logicality and invariance
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homogeneous+space"}> homogeneous space
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystallographic+group"} crystallographic group
          %h2#references References
          %h3#kleins_original_and_historical_context Klein’s original and historical context
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li#Klein1872
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Felix+Klein"}> Felix Klein
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vergleichende+Betrachtungen+%C3%BCber+neuere+geometrische+Forschungen"} Vergleichende Betrachtungen über neuere geometrische Forschungen
                (1872) Mathematische Annalen volume 43, pages 63–100 1893 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01446615"}> doi:10.1007/BF01446615
                )
              %p English translation by M. W. Haskell:
              %p
                %em> A comparative review of recent researches in geometry
                , Bull. New York Math. Soc. 2, (1892-1893), 215-249. (
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/bulletin-of-the-american-mathematical-society-new-series/volume-2/issue-10/A-comparative-review-of-recent-researches-in-geometry/bams/1183407629.full"}> euclid:1183407629
                , LaTeX version retyped by Nitin C. Rughoonauth:
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0807.3161"} arXiv:0807.3161
          %p Historical context and related material:
          %ul
            %li#BirkhoffBennett
              %p
                Garrett Birkhoff, M. K. Bennett,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Felix Klein and His “Erlanger Program”
                = succeed "," do
                  %em History and Philosophy of Modern Mathematics
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
